{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789425557,"nonce":"MrmDCRLpyclM6aVAhBZDSBt0MJs=","title":"wasm: scheduler and thread module on one agent, isolates on Workers","message":"The browser build has fibers only: Fiber.spawn/tick/idle/sleep/park/wake/live are stubs without the host feature, and the thread and isolate modules are not registered there. Follow Ash's wasm model (ash docs/wasm/fibers.md and threads.md):\n\n1. One agent. The scheduler and the thread module run cooperatively on it: Thread.create places the closure on the caller's own world, a Mutex/Lock/Deque wait parks the task, a release wakes it. A producer/consumer works as it does natively; nothing runs at the same time. Thread.count is 1.\n\n2. Suspension. The scheduler parks from native depth, which today needs krio stacks (sched_vm refuses without them). On wasm that is the unwind/rewind path of 407f14a, seeded from the poll sites and the wait natives, routed through one host import so JSPI can take it where present. Until then the stackless interpreter fibers can carry park as a fiber action for the interpreted tier.\n\n3. Time. std::time::Instant traps on wasm32-unknown-unknown. The timer heap and idle deadlines need an epoch clock the host publishes (Ash: krio_wasm::EpochClock, one ticker writes performance.now() into shared memory), and idle must return to the event loop instead of blocking on a condvar.\n\n4. Isolates map to Workers with memory of their own, spawned through the page (a Worker that blocks never starts its children; Ash routes spawn requests to the browser main thread). Channel copies cross with postMessage. That is the parallel piece in the browser.\n\n5. Parallel threads over shared memory (Workers over SharedArrayBuffer, atomics for wait/notify, stop-the-world through the same handshake) come after, behind the same Thread API.\n\nRelated: 407f14a (wasm fibers), 6b20a51 (M:N runtime). Public docs describe wasm by this model, not as a missing feature.","files":null}]}